  "question": {
    "text": "Amongst LiCl, RbCl, BeCl<sub>2</sub> and MgCl<sub>2</sub> the compounds with the greatest and the least ionic character, respectively are :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sZbm5",
      "text": "MgCl<sub>2</sub> and BeCl<sub>2</sub>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wVJFK",
      "text": "RbCl and MgCl<sub>2</sub>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "27wHp",
      "text": "LiCl&nbsp;and RbCl",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "j15zi",
      "text": "RbCl&nbsp;and BeCl<sub>2</sub>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(i)&nbsp;% Ionic character = 16(X<sub>A</sub>&nbsp;&ndash; X<sub>B</sub>) + 3.5 (X<sub>A</sub>&nbsp;&ndash; X<sub>B</sub>)<sup>2</sup><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>X</mtext> <mtext>Rb</mtext> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mo>&#183;</mo> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;,&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>X</mtext> <mtext>Cl</mtext> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mo>&#183;</mo> <mn>0</mn> </mrow></math>,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi>Be</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br />For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Rb</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi></math>&nbsp;the electronegativity difference is highest so having more ionic character. For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math>, electronegativity difference is the lowest so having less ionic character</p><p>Covalent character in compound depends upon the charge and size of ions. As charge in cation increases, covalent character&nbsp;increases and as size of cation increases covalent character decreases. Charge factor dominate over size factor. Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Be</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;has higher charge and smallest size therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BeCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;has maximum covalent character and least ionic character<br /><br />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
